[68.075271, "o", "cat /app/output/answer.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[68.075849, "o", "EMPLOYEE GRADE ANALYSIS REPORT\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nDATASET OVERVIEW:\r\nTotal employees analyzed: 481\r\nGrade distribution:\r\n  M1: 272 employees\r\n  M2: 101 employees\r\n  M3: 99 employees\r\n  M4: 4 employees\r\n  M5: 5 employees\r\n\r\nMETHODOLOGY:\r\n- Employee lifetime calculated from joining date to 10/25/2025\r\n- Lifetime pay = Total annual pay × Lifetime in years\r\n- Ratio = Average lifetime revenue ÷ Average lifetime pay\r\n- All calculations performed without rounding interim values\r\n\r\nDETAILED CALCULATIONS BY GRADE:\r\n\r\nGrade M1:\r\n  Number of employees: 272\r\n  Average lifetime revenue: $17,381,898.29\r\n  Average lifetime pay: $6,374,085.68\r\n  Average annual pay: $780,461\r\n  Revenue-to-pay ratio: 2.73\r\n\r\nGrade M2:\r\n  Number of employees: 101\r\n  Average lifetime revenue: $38,506,630.96\r\n  Average lifetime pay: $11,833,674.95\r\n  Average annual pay: $1,572,508\r\n  Revenue-to-pay ratio: 3.25\r\n\r\nGrade M3:\r\n  Number of employees: 99\r\n  Average lifetime revenue: $55,288,168.26\r\n  Average lifetime pay: $18,048,691.41\r\n  Average annual pay: $2,380,929\r\n  Revenue-to-pay ratio: 3.06\r\n\r\nGrade M4:\r\n  Number of employees: 4\r\n  Average lifetime revenue: $72,124,499.00\r\n  Average lifetime pay: $25,426,912.80\r\n  Average annual pay: $3,935,879\r\n  Revenue-to-pay ratio: 2.84\r\n\r\nGrade M5:\r\n  Number of employees: 5\r\n  Average lifetime revenue: $103,850,108.40\r\n  Average lifetime pay: $59,770,771.50\r\n  Average annual pay: $6,397,732\r\n  Revenue-to-pay ratio: 1.74\r\n\r\nTOP TWO GRADES WITH BEST RATIOS:\r\n1. Grade M2: 3.25\r\n2. Grade M3: 3.06\r\n\r\nCOST IMPACT OF 20% EMPLOYEE INCREASE:\r\n\r\nGrade M2:\r\n  Current employees: 101\r\n  Additional employees (20%): 20\r\n  Average annual pay per employee: $1,572,508\r\n  Additional annual cost: $31,450,165\r\n\r\nGrade M3:\r\n  Current employees: 99\r\n  Additional employees (20%): 20\r\n  Average annual pay per employee: $2,380,929\r\n  Additional annual cost: $47,618,570\r\n\r\nTotal additional annual cost: $79,068,735\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDAIONS:\r\nBased on the analysis, I recommend focusing expansion on grades M2 and M3 as they provide the highest revenue-to-pay ratios of 3.25 and 3.06 respectively. These grades generate the most revenue per dollar of compensation, making them the most cost-effective for expansion. The 20% increase would require an additional annual investment of $79,068,735."]
